# Verify Implementation

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file defines the process for verifying the completeness and correctness of front-end implementation. It should be consulted when:

- Confirming that all requirements have been implemented in the front-end codebase
- Validating components, hooks, and state management against requirements
- Ensuring proper test coverage across the front-end
- Verifying performance, accessibility, and user experience
- Preparing for deployment or implementation finalization

This file complements:
- **component-validation.md**: Component structure and quality validation
- **hook-validation.md**: Hook implementation validation
- **state-validation.md**: State management validation
- **recreate-ux-situation.md**: UX testing verification

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains the verification process for front-end implementation completeness and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter when comprehensive implementation verification is needed:

```
verify-implementation: front-end @parameters/front-end/helpers/verification/verify-implementation.mdc
```

## Command Format

```
verify-implementation: [target-directory-or-component] @parameters/front-end/helpers/verification/verify-implementation.mdc
```

## Required Context

To perform front-end implementation verification, the following context is required:

1. Access to the original requirements from the planning folder
2. Access to the implementation plan
3. Access to all implemented components, hooks, and state management
4. Understanding of the success criteria and user experience goals

## Process Steps

### 1. Requirements Review

First, review the original requirements to understand what was to be implemented:

```typescript
// Read the requirements document
read_file("planning/feature-name/requirements.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Identify success criteria
grep_search("## Success Criteria|## Objectives|## Requirements", false, "planning/feature-name/requirements.md")
```

### 2. Implementation Plan Review

Review the implementation plan to understand the proposed approach:

```typescript
// Read the implementation plan
read_file("planning/feature-name/implementation.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Identify key implementation components
grep_search("## Implementation Approach|## Components|## Features", false, "planning/feature-name/implementation.md")
```

### 3. Component Implementation Verification

Verify the implementation of React components:

```typescript
// List all components in the feature directory
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path 'front-end/src/components/FeatureName' -Recurse -Include '*.tsx' | ForEach-Object { $_.Name }", false, false)

// Check component structure
read_file("front-end/src/components/FeatureName/ExampleComponent.tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Check component test implementation
grep_search("test\\(|it\\(|describe\\(", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.test.tsx")

// Check component prop interface
grep_search("interface [A-Za-z]+Props", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")
```

### 4. Hook Implementation Verification

Verify the implementation of custom hooks:

```typescript
// List all hooks in the feature directory
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path 'front-end/src/hooks' -Recurse -Include 'use*.ts' | ForEach-Object { $_.Name }", false, false)

// Check hook implementation
read_file("front-end/src/hooks/useFeature.ts", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Check hook test implementation
grep_search("test\\(|it\\(|describe\\(", false, "front-end/src/hooks/**/*.test.ts")

// Check hook return type
grep_search("function use[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\\(.*\\): [A-Za-z<>\\[\\]{}|, ]+", false, "front-end/src/hooks/useFeature.ts")
```

### 5. State Management Verification

Verify the implementation of state management:

```typescript
// For Redux/RTK implementation
read_file("front-end/src/store/featureSlice.ts", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Check reducer implementation
grep_search("createSlice|reducers:|extraReducers:", false, "front-end/src/store/featureSlice.ts")

// Check selectors implementation
grep_search("export const select[A-Z]", false, "front-end/src/store/featureSlice.ts")

// Check state tests
grep_search("test\\(|it\\(|describe\\(", false, "front-end/src/store/**/*.test.ts")
```

### 6. UI and UX Verification

Verify the UI implementation and user experience:

```typescript
// Check for accessibility attributes
grep_search("aria-|role=", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")

// Check for responsive design patterns
grep_search("@media|sm:|md:|lg:|xl:", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")

// Check for proper loading states
grep_search("isLoading|loading|skeleton|fallback", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")

// Check for error handling
grep_search("error|catch|try", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")
```

### 7. Test Coverage Verification

Verify the test coverage of the implementation:

```typescript
// Run tests and check coverage
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run test:coverage", false, false)

// Check specific test files
list_dir("front-end/src/components/FeatureName/__tests__")

// Check API mocking
grep_search("mock\\(|jest.mock", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.test.tsx")
```

### 8. Performance Verification

Verify the performance optimization of the implementation:

```typescript
// Check for memoization
grep_search("React\\.memo|memo\\(|useMemo|useCallback", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")

// Check for optimized rendering
grep_search("React\\.lazy|Suspense|useTransition", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")

// Check for optimized state updates
grep_search("useReducer|useState\\(.*=>", false, "front-end/src/components/FeatureName/**/*.tsx")
```

## Expected Outputs

The verification process should produce:

1. A verification report indicating which aspects of the front-end implementation were verified
2. A completion assessment for each requirement
3. Identification of any missing or incomplete components
4. Confirmation of readiness for deployment or list of remaining items

## Error Handling

Common front-end implementation issues and their resolutions:

| Issue | Resolution |
|-------|------------|
| Missing components | Implement missing components according to requirements |
| Incomplete testing | Add tests for untested functionality |
| Accessibility issues | Add proper aria attributes and semantic HTML |
| Performance issues | Implement memoization and optimize rendering |
| Responsive issues | Add proper responsive design patterns |
| State management issues | Fix state update patterns and selector implementations |

## Verification Report Creation

Create a comprehensive verification report:

```typescript
